<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer sells unit to Honeywell.</title>
<headline>Sulzer sells unit to Honeywell.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sulzer AG said that it has sold its unit &quot;building automation and control systems&quot; to Honeywell Inc for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>The unit is a division of Sulzer Intra subsidiary Neef AG of Switzerland. The unit employs 30 people, who are expected to be integrated into a subsidiary of Honeywell headquartered in Wallisellen, Switzerland.</p>
<p>The transaction does not affect Neef GmbH, which is based in Karlsruhe, Germany and is involved in communications technology and networks.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
